        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kenyon%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Four pioneers platted the village in summer 1856, drawn by the region's forests, waters, and fertile fields.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofkenyon.gov/?SEC=B8E9EFF6-CE5D-4E40-80D9-B977CE2F2596"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Martin Gunderson built a prosperous mill and supplied electricity to Kenyon in 1896.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofkenyon.gov/?SEC=B8E9EFF6-CE5D-4E40-80D9-B977CE2F2596"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Kenyon boasts the Boulevard of Roses on Main Street, the centerpiece of its annual Rosefest each August.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
